---
/**
 * Terms & Conditions. A from-scratch draft of standard B2B terms for a
 * destination management company: we arrange trip services through local
 * operators for travel businesses, on the terms of each quote. No
 * consumer relationship, no software licence.
 *
 * DRAFT — must be reviewed by counsel before launch. noindex until then.
 * Reuses the article (.art-*) styles rather than inventing a new layout.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/contact';

const updated = '28 September 2026';
---

<Base title="Terms & Conditions" description="The terms governing Projectour's destination management services." noindex>
  <article class="hx hx-art">
    <p class="hx-art-m">Legal &middot; last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1 class="hx-art-t">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="hx-art-dek">
        These terms govern your use of Projectour's services. They are a working draft pending legal review — if
        you have questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    <div class="art-body">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Projectour ("we", "us") is a destination management company. We arrange and operate trip services for
        travel businesses through a network of vetted local ground operators. Our registered office is Intelak
        Hub, Offices 4, One Central, Dubai World Trade Center, Dubai, UAE.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Who these terms apply to</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are provided to businesses — travel agencies, advisors, creators and tour operators — not to
        consumers. By sending us a brief or accepting a quote, you confirm you are acting in the course of business
        and are authorised to bind the business you represent.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Quotes</h2>
      <p>
        We quote each trip on the basis of the brief you give us, at a net rate for your business. Quotes are valid
        for the period stated on the quote. Availability and pricing are only assured once re-verified with the
        operator and confirmed by us in writing after your acceptance. Where a component has changed between quote
        and confirmation, we will tell you before anything is booked.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Bookings and payment</h2>
      <p>
        A booking exists once we confirm it in writing. Deposit, balance and cancellation terms are as stated on the
        quote and may pass through the terms of the operators and suppliers involved, which we will set out where
        they apply. Payments are confirmed by us in writing; we do not treat a payment as received until we have
        confirmed it.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Changes and cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Changes after confirmation are re-quoted where they affect price or availability. Cancellation charges are as
        stated on the quote and reflect the terms of the underlying suppliers. Where we can recover a cost from a
        supplier on your behalf, we will.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Ensure information you supply about trips and travellers is accurate and lawfully shared with us.</li>
        <li>Hold the licences and consents your own business requires to sell travel.</li>
        <li>Advise travellers of passport, visa, health and insurance requirements for the destination.</li>
        <li>Not pass our net rates to travellers, or contract our operators directly for a trip we have quoted.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Neither party excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded. Otherwise, our aggregate liability in
        respect of a trip is limited to the fees you paid us for that trip, and neither party is liable for indirect
        or consequential loss. We arrange travel services; the transport, accommodation and activities themselves
        are supplied by the operators and suppliers who provide them, and responsibility for their performance rests
        with them, without limiting any responsibility we have for our own arranging services.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        Net rates, operator identities and your client details are confidential to the parties and are not disclosed
        beyond what is needed to run the trip.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; material changes will be notified to our customers in advance. Continued use of
        our services after the effective date constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Emirate of Dubai and the applicable federal laws of the United
        Arab Emirates, and the courts of Dubai have exclusive jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
